          {
            "id": "obs-7",
            "text": "Intervention: adding an explicit #[kani::unwind(N)] sized to the declared bound COMPLETELY fixes Vec, cheaply, at every size tried. The deciding factor was a symbolic loop bound that Kani's default unwind inference does not handle",
            "timestamp": 1787494479293,
            "provenance": {
              "sourceType": "intervention",
              "reliability": 1.0,
              "sourceRef": null
            },
            "clusterId": "c-7",
            "clusterMethod": "new"
          },
          {
            "id": "obs-8",
            "text": "Fixed-size arrays [T;N] verify cheaply at every N up to 16 with NO unwind annotation needed, because the bound is a compile-time constant",
            "timestamp": 1787494479328,
            "provenance": {
              "sourceType": "firsthand",
              "reliability": 1.0,
              "sourceRef": null
            },
            "clusterId": "c-8",
            "clusterMethod": "new"
          },
          {
            "id": "obs-9",
            "text": "BTreeSet has a second independent cost beyond loop bounds \u2014 its own generic insert algorithm, expensive past one element \u2014 which the unwind fix does not touch",
